-- ported from tests/cases/compiler/breakNotInIterationOrSwitchStatement2.ts
-- dropped: @target: es2015 directive (tlua defaults to latest target)
-- dropped: emit coverage (noEmit) -- the `break` is rejected for crossing a function
-- boundary, so the recovered tree emits a `break` inside `f`, which has no enclosing
-- loop and is invalid Lua.

// @noEmit: true

while true do
    function f()
        break
    end
end
